+# SPN-160 — Actionable maintenance handoff failures
+
+## 🧭 Complete diagnostic outcome
+
+**Date/status/source:** 2026-11-13, accepted registration and sequencing by the
+agent delivery manager under [standing four-persona authority](../todo/process.md#decisions).
+Integration, independent review and native acceptance remain pending. The complete
+outcome is **M, pre-launch**: preserve useful first failures at existing maintenance
+crash/handoff/readiness boundaries without changing recovery semantics. It has
+independent value even if neither original incident recurs; this is not a changed
+grading denominator or a publication exception.
+
+Actual main `7c38f7d32e6a55d8000239923113155de6a07c8c` starts the durable-phase
+transition with `control(action).catch(() => undefined)` at
+[supervisor.test.ts:1097](https://github.com/mxbaylee/spinel/blob/7c38f7d32e6a55d8000239923113155de6a07c8c/src/server/maintenance/supervisor.test.ts#L1097), then separately waits for the
+barrier. A transition rejection before that barrier loses its original failure and
+leaves the wait to report `Fixture message timed out.` This is a source-level
+fixture defect, not evidence of either historical Linux incident's cause.
+
+Options were retaining misleading failures, adding unbounded tracing or relaxed
+retries, or delivering one bounded failure-evidence contract before further recovery
+investigation. Choose the latter. Prepared local diagnostic candidate
+`44f9a5365fe290236b882606933e63b8ef317363` on
+`codex/spn-157-supervisor-handoffs` originated at base
+`ebf0842f51b60d54649cf8a03065914bec0944bf`. Its ten portable controls were reported
+passing in the implementation handoff; that is not native receiver acceptance or
+historical causal proof. This registration imports none of that code. Integrate
+current main and this registration, preserving check receipts and resource-aborted
+attempts, then review the complete candidate. The old local head is not claimed to
+be published or ready to merge.
+
+The complete diagnostic contract includes:
+
+- Report the original action/stage/bounded journal failure immediately when a
+  transition rejects before the observed barrier, preserving its cause. Tolerate
+  intended RPC rejection only after barrier observation. Remove message listener
+  and timer on barrier, early failure and timeout; handle late rejection without an
+  unhandled promise. Retain the original **10-second** deadline and crash assertions.
+- Freeze first-failure sender offer/request/send-callback/held progress and receiver
+  offer/request/accepted-handle/held-send progress. New receipts contain fixed
+  counts, booleans and machine codes only; exclude content, credentials, authority,
+  paths, transfer IDs, nonces and arbitrary IPC payloads. Public RPC errors stay
+  generic; original internal causes remain available.
+- Capture readiness phase, job phase, lastFailure and bounded controller category
+  before cleanup, including polling failure and unavailable job-state files.
+  Preserve receipts through the existing single Error.cause wrapper without getters
+  or cyclic/unbounded traversal. Missing/late observation cannot change handoff.
+- Add no protocol callback, timer or awaited work for observation. Keep authority,
+  persistence, admission, handle ownership, process containment and production
+  deadlines unchanged. No new service, blanket retries, skips, timeout increases or
+  selected-CI narrowing. Preserve first cause and cleanup on every outcome.
+
+**Complete M includes native diagnostic acceptance**, integration and current-head
+gates; local helpers alone cannot complete it. Reassess before broader protocol,
+recovery, authority or production observation work. The remaining combined effort
+is **SPN-160 M + SPN-157 L**, not a smaller total.
+
+**All four personas:** Operator gains useful bounded private evidence instead of
+misleading timeouts (**M**). Owner and Collaborator retain original-row,
+selected-candidate and fail-closed guarantees without new writable access; internal
+evidence offers indirect support benefits (**S** each), not completed recovery.
+Link guest gains no authority or management visibility, with content and identities
+excluded from new receipts (**S**). Additional bounded verification delays further
+investigation; safety is not inferred from improved diagnostics.
+
+## 🧪 Verification and the next bounded experiment
+
+Reuse existing/prepared `ownership.ts`/`.test.ts`, `supervisor-test-control.ts`/`.test.ts`,
+`supervisor.test.ts` and `ownership-fixture.ts`. Portable controls cover request/offer
+ordering; wrong/duplicate acknowledgements; zero/two-handle interruption; missing-held
+deadline; immutable late callbacks; retained parent listeners; direct/wrapped
+receipt extraction; throwing getters and cycle/depth bounds. Real temporary journal
+controls cover synchronous/asynchronous pre-barrier rejection, expected
+reached-then-crash rejection, unchanged timeout and late rejection, with zero
+residual message listeners/timers and exclusion of unrelated data.
+
+Existing CI Unit tests **recovery** owns portable files; **supervisor** owns real
+supervisor/ownership fixtures. Native acceptance retains **Node 26.13.0**,
+Tini/private PID namespace via `scripts/ci/pid-namespace.ts`, actual Linux abstract
+Unix kernel leases, IPC server handles and SQLite. Exercise interruption after
+two accepted handles, no SQLite open, original bytes retained and closed late
+handles, plus actual durable-phase and authenticated restore readiness with
+improved reporting. Preserve ownership, supervisor, journal, fixture and shared CI
+selection dependencies; selected missing, failed or cancelled work must fail its
+aggregate. No new runner or workflow; a Mac control cannot prove Linux behavior.
+
+After integration and qualifying independent exact-head reviews, first normal
+validation of the newly instrumented source is a **new bounded experiment**: same
+scenarios and budgets, improved evidence. Preserve its first outcome and snapshot
+before cleanup. A pass may not reproduce either original incident and proves no
+causal repair. A failure may improve attribution but still blocks that PR's merge.
+Further experiments need a concrete hypothesis/evidence gap; never repeat unchanged
+until green. No Docker, retired private host, paid infrastructure or other exception
+is authorized by this registration.
+
+## 🧾 Retained recovery scope and neighboring work
+
+SPN-157 remains **open, L**, with both complete original investigations and any
+demonstrated product/fixture repairs: durable-running SIGKILL/original-row/orphan
+recovery and readiness-first authenticated selected-candidate commit/release.
+Retain all authority, persistence, interruption, cleanup and actual Linux acceptance.
+SPN-157 now depends on SPN-160; **SPN-098 still depends on SPN-157**. No original
+acceptance is deleted, downsized, hidden or satisfied by instrumentation.
+
+Original failed run **43544143900**, source
+`2204b8c40ce6feb8ad03c65720c976510535ad00`, remains in the
+[immutable first-failure archive](https://github.com/mxbaylee/spinel/tree/5e1b7a9fac17c69ff9174caa9da9f8d13713737d/docs/review-assets/spn-098-failure-43544143900).
+Its successful comparator does not supersede it. Original failure stage and causal
+relationship of the observed child handoff timeout remain unknown. Unchanged
+supervisor files do not establish independence from SPN-098's broader startup/drain
+behavior. Carry original specification and split lineage into review. SPN-158's
+postcommit writable-admission oracle is a separate outcome.
+
+[SPN-123](SPN-123.md) retains its complete **L** fixed production operation/sync/
+maintenance emitter inventory, collectors/store/exports, schema/admission, privacy
+and measured off/on overhead. Internal first-failure receipts and test diagnostics
+do not fulfill that production telemetry contract or add an emitter/export service.
+Reuse privacy principles without transferring its unimplemented requirements.
+
+[SPN-128](../todo/SPN-128.md) retains its complete **L** journaled supervisor command
+to reinstall a preserved original after an interrupted activated trial, frozen
+fingerprint/fresh authority, generation reconciliation, real crash cuts and runbook.
+This ticket changes no recovery command or custody decision and claims none of its
+acceptance. The [focused registration record](grooming-maintenance-diagnostics-2026-11-13.md)
+retains allocation and bookkeeping separately from product completion.
